note
note One 32-lane tile of the OMEGA-NUMERIC reduce reference tree (ref_tile of
note src/omega_numeric_reduce.c and omega_warp_reduce_sum of
note src/omega_numeric.c). Composed after om/numeric/numeric.om. op 0 SUM and
note 3 MEAN add, 1 MAX and 2 MIN combine with the ref fmax/fmin; lanes fold
note in place at deltas 16 8 4 2 1, lane i ascending, as the C loops do.
fn tilecomb op ulong a ulong b ulong to ulong
if or eq op 0 eq op 3
ret fadd32 a b
end
if eq op 1
ret fmax32 a b
end
ret fmin32 a b
end
fn numeric_tile op ulong t view ulong 32 to ulong
v = new ulong 32 0
for i ulong 32
put v i get t i
end
d = ulong 16
for s ulong 5
for i ulong sub 32 d
put v i tilecomb op get v i get v add i d
end
d = shr d 1
end
ret get v 0
end
